#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:2
msgid "GNU/Linux & macOS"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:4
msgid "Contents"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:7
msgid "Prerequisites"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:9
msgid ""
"To use PyBaMM, you must have Python 3.10, 3.11, 3.12, 3.13, or 3.14 "
"installed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:13
msgid ""
"To install Python 3 on Debian-based distributions (Debian, Ubuntu), open a "
"terminal and run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:15
msgid ""
"sudo apt-get update\n"
"sudo apt-get install python3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:22
msgid ""
"On macOS, you can use the ``homebrew`` package manager. First, `install brew "
"<https://docs.python-guide.org/starting/install3/osx/>`__:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:25
msgid ""
"ruby -e \"$(curl -fsSL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Homebrew/install/"
"HEAD/install.sh)\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:29
msgid ""
"then follow instructions in the link on adding ``brew`` to path, and run"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:31
msgid "brew install python"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:37
msgid "Install PyBaMM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:42
msgid "User install"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:44
msgid ""
"We recommend to install PyBaMM within a virtual environment, in order not to "
"alter any distribution Python files. First, make sure you are using Python "
"3.10, 3.11, 3.12, 3.13, or 3.14. To create a virtual environment within your "
"current directory type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:51
msgid "uv venv"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:55
msgid ""
"This creates a ``.venv`` directory. You can then “activate” the environment "
"using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:57
msgid "source .venv/bin/activate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:63
msgid "virtualenv env"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:67
msgid "You can then “activate” the environment using:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:69
msgid "source env/bin/activate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:73
msgid ""
"When you are ready to exit the environment and go back to your original "
"system, just type:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:75
msgid "deactivate"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:79
msgid "PyBaMM can be installed via ``uv``, ``pip``, or ``conda``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:83
msgid "uv pip install pybamm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:89
msgid "pip install pybamm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:95
msgid "conda install -c conda-forge pybamm-base"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:99
msgid "PyBaMM’s :ref:`required dependencies <install-required-dependencies>`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:101
msgid ""
"(such as ``numpy``, ``casadi``, etc) will be installed automatically when "
"you install ``pybamm`` using ``pip`` or ``pybamm-base`` using ``conda``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:104
msgid ""
"For an introduction to virtual environments, see (https://realpython.com/"
"python-virtual-environments-a-primer/)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:110
msgid "Optional - JaxSolver"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:112
msgid "Users can install ``jax`` and ``jaxlib`` to use the Jax solver."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:116
msgid "uv pip install \"pybamm[jax]\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:122
msgid "pip install \"pybamm[jax]\""
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:126
msgid ""
"This command automatically downloads and installs ``pybamm`` and the "
"compatible versions of ``jax`` and ``jaxlib`` on your system."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:128
msgid ""
"PyBaMM's full `conda-forge distribution <index.rst#installation>`_ "
"(``pybamm``) includes ``jax`` and ``jaxlib`` by default."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:131
msgid "Uninstall PyBaMM"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:133
msgid "PyBaMM can be uninstalled by running"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:135
msgid "pip uninstall pybamm"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../source/user_guide/installation/gnu-linux-mac.rst:139
msgid "in your virtual environment."
msgstr ""
